From a98ab0b9244c5545a4fe4c0a6bc197cce45dc2d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:11:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Setup now asks for a Caddy root directory, deriving the
 standard layout

Setup previously only asked for the caddy.d (conf) directory. It now
asks for the Caddy root directory instead, and assumes the conventional
layout underneath it:

    <root>/
    |- caddy.d/    (conf_dir)
    |- data/       (certificate_dir -- Caddy's data directory, see
    |               https://caddyserver.com/docs/conventions#data-directory)
    |- logs/       (log_dir)
    |- Caddyfile   (caddyfile_path)

All four derived paths are saved to config.json. An Advanced options
accordion on the setup form (collapsed by default, placeholders update
live as the root directory is typed) lets any of them be overridden
individually if a real setup doesn't match the convention. Only conf_dir
is created automatically (same as before) -- Caddy manages its own
data/log directories and the Caddyfile isn't something this app should
be creating or touching.

Only conf_dir is actively used by the app today; certificate_dir, log_dir,
and caddyfile_path are stored for upcoming features.

Also wired the previously-inert Certificate/Logs directory fields on the
Settings > Directories tab (they existed in the markup but had no name
attributes -- they weren't submitted, let alone saved) into a proper
"update directories" form covering all five values (root_dir plus the
four derived paths), each independently editable and saved as entered
(no re-deriving from root_dir on every save, since any of them may have
been deliberately customized away from the default).

Renamed get_caddy_dir() -> get_conf_dir() and the caddy_dir variable/
template-kwarg/data-attribute throughout the codebase to conf_dir, to
match: configstore.py, blocks.py, views.py, block_form.html's
data-conf-dir attribute, and block-form.js's confDir variable.

Backward compatible: load_config() migrates a pre-existing config.json
that still only has "caddy_dir" -- it becomes conf_dir, its parent
directory becomes a best-guess root_dir, and the other three paths get
sensible defaults derived from that guess (correctable from Settings) --
transparently, on first load, with no action needed from an existing
install.

Verified: setup with just a root directory correctly derives and creates
conf_dir and saves all four paths; setup with an advanced override (e.g.
a custom conf_dir) keeps that override while still deriving the other
three from root_dir; Settings > Directories displays and correctly
updates all five values; a simulated pre-existing config.json with the
old "caddy_dir" key migrates correctly on first load (conf_dir preserved
exactly, sensible derived defaults for the rest, old key removed) without
disrupting login; setup's validation errors (missing root directory,
missing username/password) still render correctly. Ran the full
create/edit/preview/toggle regression across all five block types against
the new <root>/caddy.d layout, and pyflakes is clean.
